{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.MilnorVassilievBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.MilnorVassilievBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.FiniteTypeInvariant","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorParitySignLaw","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.brunnian_exact_leadingOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.brunnian_exact_leadingOrder","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/MilnorVassilievBridge.lean#L107-L128","doc":"**(CONDITIONAL on `BrunnianVassilievBridge`.)** Given the Milnor =\nleading-Vassiliev bridge, the `A`-component Brunnian link (`A ≥ 2`) carries a\nVassiliev invariant of order `leadingOrder A = 2(A−1)` taking value `±1` there\n(the μ̄-invariant), and every strictly-lower-order invariant vanishes on it.\n\nThis is the exact-order statement #4471's general `MilnorExactOrder` conjecture\nneeds: the leading Milnor order is *exactly* `2(A−1)` (not merely `≥`), the\nmissing refinement of `MilnorParitySignLaw`.  The only unproved input is the\nclass instance (§3b-cond). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.vassilievDegree_eq_leadingOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.vassilievDegree_eq_leadingOrder","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/MilnorVassilievBridge.lean#L100-L104","doc":"The Vassiliev degree `2(A−1)` used by the bridge class is #4471's leading\nMilnor order `leadingOrder A`. (Alignment check between the two independently\ndefined quantities.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.BrunnianVassilievBridge.vassiliev_trivial_below","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.BrunnianVassilievBridge.vassiliev_trivial_below","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/MilnorVassilievBridge.lean#L94-L94","doc":"The link is Vassiliev-trivial below degree `2(A−1)`: every invariant of\norder `< 2(A−1)` vanishes on it (first non-vanishing invariant is at\n`2(A−1)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.BrunnianVassilievBridge.muBar_realized","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.BrunnianVassilievBridge.muBar_realized","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/MilnorVassilievBridge.lean#L89-L89","doc":"At degree `2(A−1)` the Milnor μ̄-invariant is realized as a Vassiliev\ninvariant taking value `±1` on the `A`-component Brunnian link. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.BrunnianVassilievBridge.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.BrunnianVassilievBridge.mk","kind":"ctor","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/MilnorVassilievBridge.lean#L85-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.BrunnianVassilievBridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.BrunnianVassilievBridge","kind":"class","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/MilnorVassilievBridge.lean#L72-L95","doc":"**Conjecture class (primary): Milnor = leading Vassiliev for Brunnian\nlinks.** For a family `brunnian : ℕ → K` of `A`-component Brunnian links, the\nfirst non-vanishing Vassiliev invariant of `brunnian A` sits at degree exactly\n`2(A−1)` and equals `±μ̄(12…A) = ±1`:\n\n* there is an order-`≤ 2(A−1)` invariant taking value `±1` on `brunnian A`\n  (the Milnor μ̄-invariant realized as a Vassiliev invariant); and\n* every invariant of strictly lower order vanishes on `brunnian A` (the link is\n  Vassiliev-trivial below degree `2(A−1)`).\n\nHonest scope: this is the Bar-Natan / Habegger–Masbaum / Meilhan–Yasuhara\ntheorem, **open in Mathlib**; the class is content-bearing and **instance-less**.\nIt is NOT axiomatized — precisely the exact-order input #4471 needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.SymbolIsWeightSystem.weight_is_realized","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.SymbolIsWeightSystem.weight_is_realized","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/MilnorVassilievBridge.lean#L66-L66","doc":"Every weight system is realized as the symbol of some order-`≤ m`\ninvariant (universality / surjectivity of the symbol map). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.SymbolIsWeightSystem.symbol_is_weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.SymbolIsWeightSystem.symbol_is_weight","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/MilnorVassilievBridge.lean#L61-L61","doc":"Every order-`≤ m` invariant's symbol equals a weight system evaluated on\nthe chord diagram of the double-point pattern. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.SymbolIsWeightSystem.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.SymbolIsWeightSystem.mk","kind":"ctor","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/MilnorVassilievBridge.lean#L57-L57","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.SymbolIsWeightSystem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.SymbolIsWeightSystem","kind":"class","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/MilnorVassilievBridge.lean#L48-L68","doc":"**Conjecture class (primary): the symbol of a finite-type invariant is a\nweight system.** For a type `K` of knots with a `VassilievSetup S` and a chord-\ndiagram assignment `chord` (the double-point pattern of a singular object), the\ndegree-`m` symbol of every order-`≤ m` invariant descends to a weight system on\n`ChordDiagram m` modulo the 1T and 4T relations, and conversely every weight\nsystem arises as such a symbol (Kontsevich integral universality).\n\nHonest scope: this is Kontsevich's theorem, **open in Mathlib**; the class is\ncontent-bearing and **instance-less**.  It is NOT axiomatized. ","signatureChunk":0}]}